# Authentication Best Practices

## Supabase Auth Setup

- Use `@supabase/ssr` for server-side authentication
- Create separate clients for server and client components
- Never expose `service_role` key in client code
- Use environment variables for Supabase credentials
- Configure proper auth redirects
- Set up proper CORS and allowed domains

## Server-Side Authentication

- Use `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/server` in Server Components
- Check auth status in layouts for protected routes
- Use middleware for route-level protection
- Implement proper session validation
- Handle expired sessions gracefully
- Refresh tokens automatically

## Client-Side Authentication

- Use `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/client` in Client Components
- Subscribe to auth state changes with `onAuthStateChange`
- Handle loading states during auth operations
- Clear local state on logout
- Implement proper error handling
- Show appropriate feedback to users

## Protected Routes

- Implement auth checks in layout.tsx for protected sections
- Redirect unauthenticated users to login
- Show loading state while checking auth
- Handle edge cases (expired tokens, network errors)
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use middleware for app-wide protection

## Authentication Flows

- Email/Password: Validate input, handle errors, confirm email
- Magic Link: Send email, handle callback, verify token
- OAuth: Configure providers, handle callback, merge accounts
- Password Reset: Send reset email, validate token, update password
- Email Verification: Send confirmation, handle callback
- Account Updates: Re-authenticate for sensitive operations

## Session Management

- Store sessions in HTTP-only cookies
- Use Supabase SSR for automatic token refresh
- Handle session expiry gracefully
- Implement proper logout (clear cookies and local state)
- Don't store sensitive data in localStorage
- Validate sessions on every protected request

## Security Best Practices

- Always validate auth on server-side
- Never trust client-side auth state alone
- Implement CSRF protection
- Use secure, HTTP-only cookies
- Validate email addresses before signup
- Implement rate limiting for auth endpoints
- Log security events (failed logins, password changes)

## Error Handling

- Show user-friendly error messages
- Don't expose internal error details
- Handle network errors gracefully
- Implement retry logic for transient failures
- Log errors for monitoring
- Provide helpful recovery steps

## User Experience

- Show loading states during auth operations
- Implement proper redirects after auth actions
- Remember user's intended destination
- Show success feedback after operations
- Handle auth errors gracefully
- Implement proper accessibility for forms

## Authorization Patterns

- Check user roles and permissions server-side
- Use Row Level Security (RLS) in Supabase
- Implement proper access control checks
- Don't rely on UI hiding for security
- Validate permissions before data access
- Use Supabase policies for database security
